np"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"HMUs5NoOaX"}],"key":"quUFBUSrOT"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"BXemeb75if"}],"key":"twnE5cQhvj"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"lD05R7rsGk"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"ys15KlMhEl"}],"key":"PJ7aNmQrvs"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"ZP0g7hr92W"}],"key":"HDxiZyIJfD"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.lock-files.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"Jq4GW6KSwc"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"uGcE1G2LrV"}],"key":"Mg7Dcfq1t5"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"LczVfFQbQ0"}],"key":"um5WoU9lbf"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"qSqzZPzSKs"}],"key":"q9CBGRbZix"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"G2WFUqCc7Z"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"cn5DosmZQu"}],"key":"Bliljk92D0"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"CQmr8kbtvx"}],"key":"afq2AdpeaA"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jet-lag.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"t8qsVwRurq"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"T4jNNdsteR"}],"key":"Qi3P1FRY6C"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"Vb9Cx1DN6f"}],"key":"V1jVSrc0kX"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"wbI0zJiEvZ"}],"key":"lAckO7Y2od"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"IF0qlf8SB7"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"yRwBRqu973"}],"key":"cYjw06VREG"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"dKRqXEBfgU"}],"key":"LzxN0BVoVw"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.fund-systems-not-developmend.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"I4AGZnxsF9"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"RAn1cUXD4f"}],"key":"zwQr8cReMi"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"sc0Ul0JoyT"}],"key":"TrsOYkJpdz"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"SAEBoy9yxP"}],"key":"SGycps36FY"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"vkP02ibzM8"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"NTyximoFa9"}],"key":"O6BQKb7vtP"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"dAEechfoFx"}],"key":"LWGj0SvqBL"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.more-contributors.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"ZbUR1DC0gJ"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"TtPednvQxZ"}],"key":"A8l5Oofu03"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"pRbCiJBOIN"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"U8md1TSezf"}],"key":"hnS7C9f171"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"FqFUq61x9H"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"vxoOpZJhui"}],"key":"hZMw0i0GlB"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"X2h8xavtCR"}],"key":"vqdER0p1q2"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"RWrkwsRm65"}],"key":"LL3Zkjh8ra"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"m2phhKodMp"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"UY9eRVUOFH"}],"key":"dYQoE04QOd"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"ajTueeh6ey"}],"key":"ZzPy8pN0HA"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jupyter-org-structure.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"PyzgnsW6QV"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"h7ZZi92eWx"}],"key":"B6Xtlb9x4V"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"tYCWnRnouq"}],"key":"tETZIOnZzZ"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"VrpvBJTgfQ"}],"key":"n6xmrKweTe"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"Yw4nhSeJHy"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"fO6aE4a8ly"}],"key":"aIwGli4ZBf"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"vlQLgTlhtt"}],"key":"Ju9OvG7HMh"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.os-support.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"Q062aWPr4S"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"ZfC84N2xcR"}],"key":"h9YUsAoKng"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"AUaa31NZYR"}],"key":"TErzqLuEl3"},{"type":"f